[center][size=6][b]Recipe Pinner[/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=4][b]Your crafting companion for Valheim[/b][/size][/center]

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/hero.gif?raw=true[/img][/center]
[center][size=2]Shown with a larger HUD and a solid background, both of which are settings. By default the pins are smaller and half-transparent.[/size][/center]

[b]Valheim only tells you what you are missing while you are standing at the bench. Recipe Pinner tells you in the forest.[/b]

Pin any recipe or build piece to your HUD and what it still needs stays in front of you — counting down as you gather, turning green the moment you can craft it. Group a whole project into a single pin, and let it count the chests around you too.

[quote][b]Built for Valheim 1.0.[/b] This build cannot run on 0.221.x. If you are still on an older game version, stay on Recipe Pinner 1.3.2.[/quote]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]⭐ What It Does[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]📍 Pin it, then watch it fill up[/b][/size]

Hover a crafting recipe or a Hammer build piece, press the Pin key, and it lands on your HUD with everything it needs. From then on the numbers follow you: they climb as you pick things up, and the row turns green the moment that material is covered. Nothing to open, nothing to check.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/Vertical.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

Press the key again on the same recipe to pin a second copy, a third, a tenth — every total scales with it.

Pin something more than once and each row also shows what [b]one[/b] of them costs, in brackets. Ten stone axes need fifty wood, so with eight in your bag the row reads:

[quote][font=Courier New]8/50(5)[/font] — [b]8[/b] you have · [b]50[/b] for all ten · [b](5)[/b] for one[/quote]

The total stays red because fifty is far off, while [font=Courier New](5)[/font] turns green the moment you can afford a single axe. That is the difference between "I can't do this yet" and "I can make one right now", and you get it without doing arithmetic.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/SingleUnit.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

Your Pin and Unpin keys appear in Valheim's own button-hint bar, next to Move and Use, and follow your keys if you rebind them — so the control is discoverable without opening a config file. The Unpin hint stays hidden until there is actually something it can remove.

Upgrades can be pinned the same way, and the pin shows what that next level actually costs. Pin one at the [b]Forge of Potential[/b] and it asks for the Idol the Forge charges instead of the ordinary materials — including the levels past an item's usual cap that only the Forge can reach.

[size=4][b]🧩 Turn a whole project into one pin[/b][/size]

An armour set is not one recipe. Pin each piece separately and your HUD fills up while the thing you actually want to know — what the whole project costs — is written nowhere.

Select them in the [b]My Pins[/b] panel and combine them into a named [b]group[/b]. The group becomes a single HUD pin with one merged material list — the running total for the entire project, in one place.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/PinGroups.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

Expand the group in the [b]My Pins[/b] panel and every member shows its own materials underneath its name, which answers the question a merged list never can: [b]which one of these can I make right now?[/b]

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/GroupMembers.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

From the panel you can also:

[list]
[*]Change how many copies of a recipe you want, or remove it.[/*]
[*]Adjust an individual member's count inside a group.[/*]
[*]Disband a group back into separate pins, keeping every recipe.[/*]
[*]Put the same recipe in more than one project — duplicate pins can be split between groups.[/*]
[/list]

Groups earn their keep on armour sets, station upgrades, building projects and food prep. A big one switches to a compact grid so it does not swallow the HUD, and whatever still does not fit is folded into a single [font=Courier New]+N[/font] cell — N more materials than the pin has room to show. When a group is your only pin, it skips that limit and shows everything, which quietly turns it into a permanent shopping list.

[size=4][b]📋 Count the chests, not just your pockets[/b][/size]

The [b]Gathering List[/b] adds up everything your pins need and shows one combined total — what to bring back from the trip, rather than what each recipe wants separately. It snaps alongside an open chest, so you can see what you still need while you are moving things around.

Turn on the [b]Chest Scanner[/b] in the config ([font=Courier New]EnableChestScanning[/font]) and the nearby chests count too. Then the colours on your pins tell you three different things:

[list]
[*]🟢 [b]Green[/b] — you have it on you.[/*]
[*]🟡 [b]Yellow[/b] — you have it, but it is in a chest nearby.[/*]
[*]🔴 [b]Red[/b] — you do not have it.[/*]
[/list]

Yellow is the useful one: it is the difference between "go mine more copper" and "walk ten steps".

It is off by default, and it only ever reads — it never moves, takes or touches anything in a chest.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/Chest.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]🖥️ Gets out of the way[/b][/size]

Pins move themselves depending on what you are doing: a normal spot while you are exploring, the bottom right when your inventory or a chest is open, moved aside while you are sailing, and clear of Valheim's button-hint bar when that is on. Pin more than fits on one screen and the list pages instead of growing.

If you use [b]MyLittleUI[/b], the layout goes horizontal on its own to stay out of its way. If you prefer a different spot entirely, every layout's position is a setting.

Each pin can also carry a coloured bar along its edge — ready or not ready — so the answer is available from the corner of your eye, without reading a single number.

Almost none of this is fixed. The settings cover the hotkeys, the layouts and where they sit, HUD scale, fonts, colours, icon sizes, how many pins fit on a page, when a group goes compact, and whether a recipe unpins itself once you have crafted it — and [b]nearly every one applies the moment you change it.[/b] Open the config with the HUD on screen and you can watch a slider move the pins.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/Inventory.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]🌍 Every language Valheim speaks[/b][/size]

Recipe Pinner follows the language you play in. There is nothing to set and nothing to download — pick your language in Valheim, and the pins, the panel, the dialogs and the hints all follow.

Some of those translations were AI-assisted, so one may read awkwardly in your language. Please report it if it does — or fix it yourself and keep the fix. The language files sit in a plain folder next to the mod, one line per piece of text, and a text editor is the only tool you need.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/Languages.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]✅ Requirements And Compatibility[/b][/size]

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td]
[td][b]Valheim 1.0 or newer[/b] — see the note at the top if you are on an older one.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]Needs[/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/3605]BepInExPack Valheim[/url] 5.4.2351 or newer, and nothing else.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]Install on[/b][/td]
[td]Your own game only. Recipe Pinner draws a HUD and reads your own inventory — it sends nothing over the network, so it works in multiplayer whether or not anyone else has it, and a dedicated server does not need it.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]Optional[/b][/td]
[td][url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/Azumatt/Official_BepInEx_ConfigurationManager/]Configuration Manager[/url], to change every setting in-game.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]Other UI mods[/b][/td]
[td]The horizontal HUD layout exists for MyLittleUI users, and the My Pins button can be moved out of another mod's way. If something fights with it, please report it and name the other mod.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🔧 Installation[/b][/size]

[b]With a mod manager[/b] — [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/vortex]Vortex[/url], [url=https://www.overwolf.com/app/thunderstore-thunderstore_mod_manager]Thunderstore Mod Manager[/url], [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/ebkr/r2modman/]r2modman[/url] or [url=https://github.com/Kesomannen/gale/releases]Gale[/url] (recommended). Easiest, and it handles the dependency for you.

[b]By hand[/b] — install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/3605]BepInExPack Valheim[/url] first, then put [font=Courier New]RecipePinner.dll[/font] and the [font=Courier New]RecipePinner_languages[/font] folder together in [font=Courier New]Valheim/BepInEx/plugins/RecipePinner/[/font]:

[code]BepInEx/
└── plugins/
    └── RecipePinner/
        ├── RecipePinner.dll
        └── RecipePinner_languages/
            ├── English.json
            ├── Turkish.json
            └── ...[/code]

[font=Courier New]RecipePinner_languages[/font] has to stay next to the DLL.

[b]Updating[/b] — install the new version over the old one. Your pins, groups and their order load unchanged. Anything worth knowing for the version you are coming from is in the changelog on this page, or [url=https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/docs/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url] on GitHub.

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🕹️ Getting Started[/b][/size]

[b]Pin something.[/b] Open a crafting station or the Hammer's build menu, hover a recipe or a piece, and press [font=Courier New]Mouse Wheel Click[/font]. It lands on your HUD with its materials. Press the same key again on the same recipe to pin a second copy; hold [font=Courier New]Left Shift[/font] and press it to take one back off.

[b]Open the panel.[/b] With your inventory open, click the pin icon just left of the crafting panel's [b]CRAFT[/b] tab — hover it and it reads [b]MY PINS[/b]. That is everything you have pinned, each row with its own materials, and the controls to change a count or remove a pin.

[center][img]https://github.com/KadrioS/RecipePinner/blob/main/assets/images/MyPinsButton.png?raw=true[/img][/center]

[b]Group them into a project.[/b] In My Pins, click [b]Group[/b], select at least two pins, confirm, and give the group a name. They collapse into a single HUD pin with one merged material list. Expand the group again and each member shows its own materials; [b]Disband[/b] turns them back into separate pins whenever you want.

That is all you need to start. Everything below is controls, settings and the finer details.

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🎮 Controls[/b][/size]

[table]
[tr][th]Action[/th][th]Default[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Pin recipe / add count[/td][td][font=Courier New]Mouse Wheel Click[/font][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Decrease / remove pin[/td][td][font=Courier New]Left Shift[/font] + [font=Courier New]Mouse Wheel Click[/font][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Toggle HUD overlay[/td][td][font=Courier New]F7[/font][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Toggle Gathering List[/td][td][font=Courier New]F8[/font][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Cycle HUD pages[/td][td][font=Courier New]Left Alt[/font][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Clear all pins[/td][td][font=Courier New]P[/font] (press twice)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Open My Pins panel[/td][td]Pin icon beside the [b]CRAFT[/b] tab, inventory open[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Every one of these can be rebound in the config. They are keyboard and mouse only for now — gamepad support is on the ideas list, so a controller player will not be able to pin anything yet.

Clearing all pins asks before it does anything: press the key once to arm it, then again within two seconds. The My Pins panel also has an info button that shows your current keys in-game, so you never have to come back here for them.

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

