[size=5][b]⚙️ Configuration[/b][/size]

Install [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/Azumatt/Official_BepInEx_ConfigurationManager/]Official BepInEx ConfigurationManager[/url] and press [font=Courier New]F1[/font] in-game to reach everything with the HUD still on screen. Editing [font=Courier New]BepInEx/config/com.Kadrio.RecipePinner.cfg[/font] by hand works too, and deleting that file restores every default on the next launch.

[b]Every category, and what it covers:[/b]

[spoiler]
[table]
[tr][th]Section[/th][th]What it covers[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][b]General[/b][/td][td]Enable the mod, language override, layout mode, pin limit, pins per page, auto-unpin after crafting or building[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Controls[/b][/td][td]Every hotkey: pin, unpin, toggle visibility, Gathering List, page switch, clear all[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Chest Scanner[/b][/td][td]Whether nearby chests count toward your materials, plus scan range and interval[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]HUD Appearance[/b][/td][td]UI scale, background opacity, font sizes, recipe/material/group icon sizes, the craft-readiness bar, the single-unit bracket[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Colors[/b][/td][td]The three material states, the recipe name, and both readiness-bar colors[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Pagination[/b][/td][td]Page dot size, spacing, color and inactive opacity[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Gathering List[/b][/td][td]Turn it on, open it automatically, column count, font sizes, and where it sits beside an open chest[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Groups[/b][/td][td]When a group switches to the compact grid, how many rows it may use, and the group icon's font size[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]My Pins Panel[/b][/td][td]Panel width, height and position, the button's position, size and icon color, and the size of the materials shown on each row[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Layout (Vertical)[/b][/td][td]List width, pin spacing, position[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Layout (Horizontal - Map Side)[/b][/td][td]Column width, pin spacing, position[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Layout (Horizontal - Bottom Right)[/b][/td][td]Column width, pin spacing, position, and whether the list lifts clear of Valheim's button-hint bar[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Debug[/b][/td][td]Verbose logging. Off by default; turn it on before reporting a bug[/td][/tr]
[/table]
[/spoiler]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]❓ FAQ[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Will this mod disable my achievements?[/b][/size]

Valheim switches achievements off while [b]any[/b] mod is installed. That is the game's own check and every mod trips it, Recipe Pinner included — but it is not permanent, and it is not something the mod does to you. The modded flag only exists in the running game, so removing your mods turns achievements back on.

What [i]is[/i] permanent is the game's own cheat marking: console cheats are recorded on your character, spawned items stay marked as cheated for as long as you keep them, and world modifiers are recorded on the world. Recipe Pinner does none of these — it reads your inventory and draws a HUD. It runs no console commands, spawns nothing and changes no world setting.

Since Valheim 1.0.12 you can also opt back in while still modded. With the console enabled, run:

[font=Courier New]yesiuseddevcommandsbutiwantmyachievementsanyway[/font]

The setting is saved on your character, so once is enough.

[size=4][b]Do I need this on a server, or do my friends need it?[/b][/size]

No to both. Recipe Pinner draws a HUD and reads your own inventory, and it sends nothing over the network. Install it on your own game only: it works in multiplayer whether or not anyone else has it, and a dedicated server does not need it.

[size=4][b]Does it work with modded recipes?[/b][/size]

Yes. Anything that shows up in a crafting station's list or the Hammer's build menu can be pinned, including recipes and pieces other mods add — Recipe Pinner reads what the game shows you, not a list of vanilla items. If a modded recipe pins wrongly, please report it and name the mod.

[size=4][b]The Pins button overlaps something. Can I move it?[/b][/size]

Yes. [font=Courier New]MyPinsButtonPosition[/font] sets where it sits and [font=Courier New]MyPinsButtonSize[/font] how big it is, and both apply the moment you change them — open the config while the inventory is on screen and you can watch the button move. X grows to the left and Y grows upward.

If another mod rearranges the crafting panel, this is the setting that gets the button out of its way.

[b]More questions:[/b]

[spoiler]
[b]Does it craft from chests, like the craft-from-container mods?[/b]
No. The Chest Scanner only counts what is in nearby chests, so your numbers tell the whole story. Crafting still takes from your inventory exactly as it normally does.

[b]Will it slow my game down?[/b]
It is light. The counting only reruns when your inventory changes, and the Chest Scanner — the only part that looks at the world around you — is off by default and checks on an interval rather than every frame.

[b]Is it safe to remove?[/b]
Yes. Your pins are kept in their own files under [font=Courier New]BepInEx/config/RecipePinner_Data/[/font], and the mod adds nothing to your world or your character, so uninstalling it leaves both untouched.

[b]Does the Chest Scanner touch what is in my chests?[/b]
No. It only reads — it never moves, takes or rearranges anything — and it stays off until you turn it on. Its range and interval are both settings.

[b]Are pins shared between my characters?[/b]
No. Each character has its own pins, saved separately. Switching characters loads that character's own list.

[b]Does it work with MyLittleUI?[/b]
Yes. Auto-Detect switches to the horizontal layout when MyLittleUI is installed, reading MyLittleUI's own settings to decide.

[b]Why does my group pin show +N instead of all its materials?[/b]
A group with many different materials switches to a compact grid, and that grid is capped so one large group cannot stretch the pins beside it. Raise the cap with [font=Courier New]GroupCompactMaxRows[/font], or change when compact mode starts with [font=Courier New]GroupCompactThreshold[/font]. When a group is your only pin, it never shows +N.

[b]Can I force a particular language?[/b]
Yes, with the [font=Courier New]LanguageOverride[/font] setting. Left alone, the mod follows Valheim's language.

[b]How do I fix a bad translation myself?[/b]
Open the matching [font=Courier New].json[/font] in [font=Courier New]BepInEx/plugins/RecipePinner/RecipePinner_languages/[/font], edit the text on the right of each line, and save. Leave placeholders like [font=Courier New]{0}[/font] alone — they are replaced with numbers and key names at runtime.

[b]Why did some config settings reset after updating?[/b]
Version 1.3.0 reorganized the config categories, so a setting that moved may not have kept its old value. If you are coming from 1.2.x, launch once and glance over the layout, hotkey, Chest Scanner and Gathering List sections. Nothing is broken if you skip it — you may just be running a default you did not choose.
[/spoiler]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🐞 Known Issues[/b][/size]

[b]With Quick Stack Store installed, its container buttons land on the Gathering List.[/b] QSS places its buttons to the right of the container window, which is exactly where the list snaps when you open a chest, so the two end up on top of each other. Until it is fixed properly, raising the X value of [font=Courier New]ContainerGatheringListPosition[/font] moves the list clear of them.

Anything else, please report it — see [b]Support And Feedback[/b] below.

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🧭 Future Ideas[/b][/size]

Things I may build next. No promises on any of them, and the one at the bottom shows how this list is meant to work.

[list]
[*][b]Group readiness bar:[/b] split a group's accent bar into one segment per member, so a single glance tells you which recipes in the project are already craftable.[/*]
[*][b]Chest Scanner in the readiness bar:[/b] turn the bar yellow when a recipe is craftable only with nearby chest contents, matching how the material counts already behave.[/*]
[*][b]Hold-to-pin quantity:[/b] hold the Pin key to choose how many copies to pin, instead of pressing it once per copy.[/*]
[*][b]Station requirement on the pin:[/b] show which crafting station a recipe needs and at what level, so a pin can tell you the materials are ready but the station is not.[/*]
[*][b]Ready-made pin sets:[/b] pin a whole kit at once — an iron set, a bronze set — instead of picking the recipes one by one.[/*]
[*][b]Share a group to chat:[/b] send a group's material list into the chat window so a co-op party knows what to collect.[/*]
[*][b]Pinned recipe highlight:[/b] mark pinned recipes inside the crafting panel. This one may not be feasible.[/*]
[*][b]Gamepad support[/b], material-gathered notifications, auto-sorting craftable pins to the top, chest highlighting, VNEI, and more compatibility work with other UI and crafting mods.[/*]
[*]✅ [s][b]Pin keybind hint:[/b] show the Pin control in the game's own hint bar, next to Move and Use.[/s] Shipped in 1.5.0.[/*]
[/list]

[center]──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[/center]

[size=5][b]🤖 AI-Assisted Development[/b][/size]

Recipe Pinner is built with significant AI assistance, most heavily from 1.3.0 onward, when My Pins and Pin Groups grew past what I could finish on my own. I would call it AI-assisted rather than AI-generated, and I would rather say so up front than leave anyone to guess.

What it is not is unattended. Every release is reviewed, tested in game and judged by me before it goes out, and anything that breaks is mine to answer for.

